WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
We are now moving into the next section, bleeding and wounds.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Before you ever touch a wound, whether it's minor like a small scrape or major and life-threatening,

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
remember to scan your surroundings for danger and make sure you have your gloves and other PPE on.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.000
As we walk through these next few slides, I want you to keep one word fixed in your mind, pressure.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.000
That is going to be your most powerful tool for stopping blood loss.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:33.000
To help you get a feel for how this works in a real situation, your instructor may pass out some materials to everyone now.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Each of you should have a pair of gloves, two squares of gauze and one roll of gauze.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Go ahead and get those ready at your stations. We'll be using them in the upcoming slides.

